x ::= until-16\n","grammar_lazy":true,"grammar_triggers":[{"type":1,"value":"<seed:tool_call>\n"}],"preserved_tokens":[3,4,7,8,157],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<seed:bos>assistant\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"next_token":[{"has_next_token":false,"has_new_line":false,"n_remain":-1,"n_decoded":0}],"prompt":"<seed:bos>system\nYou are a software engineer. Your workspace directory is /tmp/runs/smokes/seed-q4/message-board/execution/runs/201/app. Implement the task described by the user by creating files in the workspace using the provided tools. Work until the task is complete, then call finish. Use only the tools provided to you.\n\nEnvironment: the tools listed in this request are the complete set available to you. Tools not listed do not exist in this environment and cannot be installed or obtained. Review what is available and use whatever helps you complete and check your work. If execution tools are provided, they give you a live development environment: the commands you run through them execute for real in your workspace, on a machine with Node.js and npm installed and the npm registry reachable, so the packages you install and the servers you start are real. If no installation or execution tools are provided, author every required file completely from first principles; dependencies declared in package.json files are provisioned by the environment after you finish.\n\nFunction:\ndef read_file(path: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Read a file in the workspace.\n\n    Args:\n    - path (str) [必填]: \n\n    \"\"\"\n\nFunction:\ndef write_file(path: str,content: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Create or overwrite a file. Any missing parent directories in `path` are created automatically.\n\n    Args:\n    - path (str) [必填]: